  "description": "OSI session layer (ISO 8326/8327), profiled to the kernel + duplex functional units MMS/61850 actually uses: SPDU parsing (its own SPDU/parameter encoding, not ASN.1 BER), CONNECT/ACCEPT/REFUSE, DATA TRANSFER, FINISH/DISCONNECT, and ABORT handling. Uses Span<byte> for framing like the BER-based layers above it, but does not depend on Iec61850.Asn1Ber.",
